{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>In order to establish you, etc.</b> That is, the reason I seek to multiply punishments and curses is in order to establish you for Him as a people, so that you will not disbelieve in Him — for you will fear the severity of the curses that you will incur should you disbelieve in His divinity — and thereby you will endure as the people of HaShem." "<b>Further,</b> it intends to give a reason for the covenant of mutual responsibility (arevut), so that no person should say: ״Why should HaShem do thus to His servants, to make their yoke heavy by binding them for the deeds of others?״ Therefore He said that Elohim intended it for good — in order to establish you for Him as a people. That is, were it not for this mutual responsibility, Israel would fall away step by step: today one sins in something light, tomorrow in something severe, and they would gradually slip away from the holy congregation until Israel would cease to be the people of HaShem. But by making them guarantors for one another, they will take heed not to commit even one light transgression as though it were severe, and they will endure as a treasured people. From this you learn that every deed of HaShem is nothing but for our good, to establish us."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:19:58.819238694Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}